From a deployment viewpoint, three key challenges remain: (1) **Computational burden** – _SO_ (3)-equivariant representations (tensors, spherical-harmonic features, etc.) inflate FLOPs and memory usage;

(2) **Quantization brittleness** – naively applying standard 8-bit quantization or post-training quantization (PTQ) to equivariant GNNs can distort vector feature directions and magnitudes, causing significant accuracy drops and broken equivariance;

(3) **Uniform treatment of scalar/vector features** – treating all features identically during quantization is suboptimal, since invariant scalars and equivariant vectors have very different distributions and roles, requiring calibrated handling. This work targets these gaps with an equivariance-aware quantization framework that preserves symmetry and accuracy while enabling real-time low-bit inference;
